  "notes": "Multi-stage protocol test points (TP_k##_##) on 279 cells; experiments_meta.csv and each *_meta.txt (author files in the raw data) give the laboratory, chamber temperature, SOC and DOD, and C-rates per cell. Cell model named on the landing page and in the paper abstract; specs from the manufacturer datasheet. The recorded cathode (NMC, from the registry) differs from the NCA the Stanford dataset_26 landing page calls this same Samsung INR21700-50E - not resolved here; flag for review. Experiment-table labels repeat across two stages. Matching now requires the testpoint label, laboratory and internal cell serial together: 230 exact matches, with 93 prior stage assignments corrected; 49 inconsistent raw/table identities retain their raw metadata but no experiment assignment. The 279 archives are extracted experiment entities, while raw laboratory/internal-serial pairs number 261; physical cell reuse across stages is unresolved. Rate maxima 1C/2C remain supported by the matched author-table rows. Charging profile: the cycling units repeat blocks of charges at several C-rates. Paper (read in full): the paper states neither the cathode chemistry nor a nominal voltage, so the NMC/NCA question above stays open and nominal_voltage_V stays null. Ambient temperatures 10, 23, 35 and 45 °C across three labs (SIE, INT, HM) on BaSyTec testers; RPTs at 23 °C; capacity step CC C/2 charge to 4.2 V (C/20 cut-off) and CC 1C discharge to 2.5 V (C/20 cut-off). Rate combinations: besides the CC-CV C/2 charge with CC-CV 1C discharge of the capacity tests, the cycling cells run plain CC charge and CC discharge (the authors kept the SOC window at 20-80% to avoid CV), at the 39 distinct (charge, discharge) pairs of experiments_meta.csv, charge 0.2 to 1.0C and discharge 0.2 to 2.0C; these C-rates are the authors' table values."
